# Enchanted Evening ("All permanents are enchantments in addition to their other types"), then Opalescence ("Each other
# non-Aura enchantment is a creature ... with base power and base toughness each equal to its mana value"). Layer 4: both
# effects apply there, and Opalescence's depends on Enchanted Evening's - applying Evening's changes what Opalescence's
# applies to (CR 613.8a) - so Evening's applies first whatever the timestamps; here it is the earlier one as well (the other
# order is enchanted-evening-after-opalescence-...). Every permanent but Opalescence is then a non-Aura enchantment, and a
# creature. Layer 7b: each has base power and toughness equal to its mana value (CR 202.3). The lands and the Moxes (mana
# value 0) are 0/0 and are put into their owners' graveyards (CR 704.5f): Bot1's Plains and Moxes, Bot2's Islands and its
# Ornithopter (a 0/2 artifact creature of mana value 0, now 0/0). Enchanted Evening is a 5/5 ({3}{W/U}{W/U}: CR 202.3e,
# a hybrid symbol counts one). Opalescence is no creature ("other"), so it stays a plain enchantment.

